From: momokind <momokind2002@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Pack the tone-mapping output in 8 or 10 bits

The non-tunnel output modes (HDR10 / SDR / WCG-SDR) were described as
XRGB2101010 but P2 still quantised to 8 bits and Kodi still imported an
XRGB8888 dma-buf. Add pi_options.output_bits: 8 keeps XRGB8888, 10 packs
XRGB2101010 (X2R10G10B10: R<<20 | G<<10 | B), selected in P2 by a
specialisation constant so only one packing survives compilation. The DV
tunnel stays 8-bit, as its standard requires.

Kodi chooses the depth from the mode's link budget: 10-bit RGB needs
1.25x the 8-bit TMDS clock, and the RK3588 HDMI glue runs TMDS only
(no FRL). The dither amplitude follows the packing (1/255 or 1/1023).

diff --git a/engine/pi_engine.h b/engine/pi_engine.h
--- a/engine/pi_engine.h
+++ b/engine/pi_engine.h
@@ -85,8 +85,9 @@
 
 /* Output signal format produced by P2:
  *   DV_STANDARD  8-bit RGB HDMI tunnel (default, existing behaviour)
- *   HDR10        10-bit XRGB2101010 ST.2084 PQ BT.2020
- *   SDR          10-bit XRGB2101010 BT.2390 L1 tone-mapped SDR / WCG-SDR */
+ *   HDR10        ST.2084 PQ BT.2020, packed as output_bits says
+ *   SDR          BT.2390 L1 tone-mapped SDR / WCG-SDR, packed as output_bits says
+ * output_bits: 8 packs XRGB8888, 10 packs XRGB2101010 (the DV tunnel is always 8). */
 enum pi_output_mode { PI_OUT_DV_STANDARD = 0, PI_OUT_HDR10 = 1, PI_OUT_SDR = 2 };
 
 /* Target colour gamut for PI_OUT_SDR. */
@@ -123,6 +124,7 @@
     unsigned measure;             /* PI_MEASURE_* */
     unsigned ablate;              /* p2_pack.frag ABLATE: measurement only */
     enum pi_output_mode output_mode;
+    unsigned output_bits;         /* non-tunnel packing: 8 XRGB8888, 10 XRGB2101010 */
     unsigned target_nits;         /* 0: auto (HDR10 passthrough / SDR 203 nits); else 50..10000 */
     enum pi_sdr_gamut sdr_gamut;
     enum pi_sdr_gamma sdr_gamma;

